// Mutations of the ct code in the editor (§7.4): VM after editing executes the ct module
// (elaboration) - the node changed by it is shown to be changed; editing the source rolls back its
// mutations and executes again, removing the source rolls back:
//  
// 
// Elaboration - by pausing the set (idle), as well as checking. The
// client text is checked with projection after each response.
// program: editor_ct.vish
open_view module
// expect: struct point { i64 x; i64 y; i64 z = 7; }
// 7 → 8 - The mutation is rolled back and made anew
pointer 1 @7:2 0 0
key 1 Delete
idle
// expect: i64 z = 0;
key 1 8
// expect: курсор:   p.items = array{...p.items, ast.variable{"z", ast.name{"i64"}, ast.int{8‸}}};
idle
// expect: struct point { i64 x; i64 y; i64 z = 8; }
// The source is no longer a ct code (ct → xct): the mutation rolls back, the z field is no
pointer 1 @ct:2 0 0
key 1 x
// expect: struct point { i64 x; i64 y; }
// expect-not: i64 z = 8; }
// ct again - the field is back
key 1 Backspace
idle
// expect: struct point { i64 x; i64 y; i64 z = 8; }
// Canon and journal: playback - the same projection and the same conclusion (draft - one edit)
key 1 Escape
roundtrip
// expect: roundtrip: совпадает
